    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Wc1BXxTvTxzHC4bZMrZzXJ)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Order: independent, any time (branch `546-…` is from `main`)\n- Depends on: nothing; uses `sp-notes-open--info` and `sp-notes-filing-protected-files`, already on main\n- If merged first or last: no breakage; the `d` key in `lem+notes-keys` is free on main\n- Conflicts with: #540 (both add a line to `docs/architecture/global-keymap-namespaces.org`, different hunks; keep both)\n- After merging: nothing to retarget\n\n## Summary\n\n- New command `sp-notes-trash` in `sp-notes`, bound to **`C-; n d`** (`d` for delete; the free letter in the notes keymap beside `c` create and `o` open; the old Denote `n d` is gone).\n- Target: the current buffer's file; with `C-u`, a file picked from `sp-notes-dir`.\n- Confirmation shows the note title and path, and warns about unsaved changes.\n- Backlinks: other notes linking to any `:ID:` in the file (via `vulpea-db-query-links-to`) are listed (first 5) and a typed `yes` is required.\n- After the move succeeded: kills the buffer, drops the ids from `org-id-locations`, and calls `vulpea-db--forget-file` so the note leaves the index and other notes' backlinks.\n- Never deletes for good: if the trash fails, nothing else changes.\n- Refuses buffers without a file, missing files, protected files (`inbox.org`, `dg-synthesis.org`) and files locked by another Emacs.\n- Trash: `move-file-to-trash` with `delete-by-moving-to-trash` on. Emacs with the NS port (Emacs Plus) uses `system-move-file-to-trash`, the Finder trash. A build without it on macOS uses the `trash` command if installed, else `~/.Trash`.\n- Docs: new section in `docs/tangles/academic/sp-notes.org`, `sp-keys.org` key list, `global-keymap-namespaces.org` notes row.\n- No CHANGELOG edit (nightly tidy).\n\n## Checks\n\n- 8 new ERT tests (trash and vulpea stubbed); 38/38 in `sp-notes-test` + `sp-keys-test` pass in batch Emacs 29.\n- `tools/check-tangle.sh`: `.el` files in this PR are the tangled output of the docs.\n- Not run on the real vault or on macOS.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Pull this branch, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`)\n- [ ] `C-; n` shows `d` in which-key as `sp-notes-trash` (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] Make a throwaway note with `C-; n c`, then `C-; n d`: prompt shows title and path; `n` keeps it\n- [ ] Repeat and answer `y`: buffer closes, note is in the Finder trash, Finder \"Put Back\" restores it (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] `C-; n o` and `C-; n n` no longer list the trashed note (index updated)\n- [ ] Edge: trash a note that another note links to: prompt lists the linking note and needs `yes`; the other note's backlinks no longer show it\n- [ ] Edge: edit the note without saving, then trash: prompt mentions unsaved changes\n- [ ] Edge: `C-u C-; n d` from a non-note buffer picks a file; `inbox.org` is refused\n- [ ] Regression: `C-; n c`, `C-; n o`, `C-; n f` still work\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard any local edits made while testing: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (and `git clean -fd` only after checking `git clean -nd`).\n- Return to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main` and `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally delete the test branch locally: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D 546-notes-trash-command`; the remote copy stays until the PR is merged or closed.\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`) so the config matches main again.\n- Restore any test note you trashed from the Finder trash (Put Back).\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAj4gwhPvJxPrg7LJv)_",
